{
  "_readme": "Canonical registry of every variable a research/pitch prompt can reference. Mirrored, without hand-edits, by src/lib/promptVariables.ts and supabase/functions/_shared/promptVariables.ts; the workspace-campaign contract script asserts all three agree, that every {{variable}} used in docs/pitch-research-prompts.json appears here, that every podcast-sourced entry is actually SELECTed by both executors, and that every run entry is assigned by the stage that claims to produce it. Groups: podcast and episode come from the Podscan catalogue, client from the client record and its AI SDR profile, run from a stage that already finished. A variable costs nothing until a prompt references it, so the rule here is to declare everything we hold rather than to curate.",
  "_excluded": "Verified against the live schema on 2026-07-29: every podcast and client column below exists and is deliberately left out. Account management and portal plumbing, not the guest: clients.notes (operator CRM freetext — a leaked strategy note reached a host once already), email, status, contact_person, first_invoice_paid_date, notifications_enabled, google_sheet_url, outreach_webhook_url, bison_campaign_id, photo_url, and every portal_*, password_*, dashboard_* and *_slug column. Our bookkeeping, not the show: podcasts.podscan_last_fetched_at, podscan_fetch_count, cache_hit_count, embedding and its metadata, id, podscan_id, created_at, updated_at. Everything else the two tables hold is offered to prompts.",
